                    {
                        "sense_id": "7c352c27-9885-3488-a368-e405a94df562",
                        "entry_id": "92f86a3f-e014-3460-be4a-ec4611c98cab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To surpass in scouting, or reconnaissance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e249a280-c1f2-4378-97d3-f0a4fa79e4e1",
                                "sense_id": "7c352c27-9885-3488-a368-e405a94df562",
                                "text": "In the Matabele campaign he had out[-]scouted the savage scouts and found his pleasure in tracking them among their native mountains, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0248e5cf-cfe3-473a-90e3-9888c038eb64",
                                "sense_id": "7c352c27-9885-3488-a368-e405a94df562",
                                "text": "A major league owner in Brooklyn, St. Louis or Chicago might not be able to outscout and outspend the Yankees. But he could find and sign gifted ballplayers in places the Yankees ignored."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "04e830a9-8233-3ccd-ba86-854855dedf1c",
                        "entry_id": "92f86a3f-e014-3460-be4a-ec4611c98cab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To overpower by disdain; to outface."
